## Shared snippet dm-check.vm (shared/vm), inlined by tools/build-widget.py at "## BW_SHARED dm-check.vm" (dmCheck).
## Checks the declared documents against the model (widgets/dmCheck/SPECIFICATION.md K3-K5, K15; docs/ARCHITECTURE.md 4).
## Needs dm-read.vm, dm-yaml.vm and dm-model.vm ($dmRoles, $dmRules, $dmUnexpLinks, $dmErrors, $dmDeclSql).
## Data, SQL forms verified on 2512 (sister repo, docCoverage): (1) the items of the declared documents, one query;
## (2) the link sources between declared documents with a link role used by the rules (DISTINCT, joins on module and
## project); their links are read with getLinkedWorkItemsStructsDirect(). Only the declared documents are read.
## Input: $dcItemCap, $dcLinkCap, $dcListCap.
## Output:
##   $dcRun (true when the checks ran), $dcNote (why not), $dcItemN, $dcLinkN, $dcUnres (unresolvable link targets),
##   $dcCapped (item or link cap reached)
##   $dcViol   list of [severity, kind, rule id, document key, item key, message]; kinds: missing-type, too-many,
##             unexpected-type, from, to, cross-pair, unpaired, unexpected-link (at most $dcListCap per rule and kind)
##   $dcViolN  map "rule|kind" -> full count;  $dcSevN map severity -> full count
##   $dcStat   map rule id -> map fc, fo (from side: checked, compliant), tc, to (to side), cross, unp, sev
##   $dcDocs   list of maps key, roles (list), items (counted), bad (items with a violation), types ("type|n;" text)
##   $dcQs     drill-down queries (K9, dmCheck 0.2): list of [rule, kind, document key, count, Lucene query] for the
##             kinds from, to (per document of the rule's side) and unexpected-type (per document). The query lists the
##             same items as the evaluation: NOT IN form verified on 2512 (dmSpike S10 runs 5 and 5b, also inside a
##             Lucene SQL:(...) restriction); count = violations of that rule, kind and document
